-&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Similar to the &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Current No Reverse With Brake &lt;/span&gt;mode, but holding full brake will switch to duty cycle mode in the reverse direction when the speed is so low that not enough brake torque can be produced. This is useful when trying to stop downhill where you normally would roll forwards slowly even at full brake. Instead, the board will start to go reverse slowly in duty cycle mode if this mode is activated.&lt;/p&gt;
+&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;电流智能反转&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
